&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Aker Systems was founded in 2017 by a team of experienced technology professionals who recognised an opportunity to provide highly secure enterprise data platforms to large organisations.&amp;nbsp; We build and operate ground-breaking, ultra-secure, high performance, cloud-based data infrastructure for the enterprise. Our proprietary technology solutions drive performance and reduce costs while helping our clients to improve the management and sharing of data across their organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2024, Aker Systems won the Breakthrough Culture Awards highlighting growth companies putting culture first. In 2020 Aker Systems was recognised as a ‘One to Watch’ on the Sunday Times Tech Track.&amp;nbsp; The Company was also recognised at the Thames Valley Tech Awards 2020; winning the Thames Valley Tech Company of the year, the Emerging Tech Company and High Growth Tech Business categories.&amp;nbsp; We encourage people of all different backgrounds and identities to apply.&amp;nbsp; We are committed to maintaining an inclusive, and supportive place for you to do your very best work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance is required for this role. If you don’t hold SC clearance, we will support you to apply assuming you have lived and worked in the UK for a minimum of 5 years.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead DevOps Engineer, you will help lead the development and implementation of secure cloud environments hosting data and batch/real-time analytical platforms for public and private sector clients, leveraging the latest commercial and open-source technologies and techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This also involves building automated deployments using configuration management technology, deploying new modules, upgrades and fixes to test and production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, test and deploy cloud-based infrastructure and applications using CI/CD and Infrastructure-as-Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the coding of custom test automation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform script maintenance and updates due to changes in requirements or implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with setup/maintenance of environments for both manual and automated testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in production support through the investigation and resolution of incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ongoing routine application maintenance tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in conducting gap analysis, identifying feasible alternative solutions, and assisting in the scope of modifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the contingency planning, including reliable backup and restore procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document functions and changes to new or modified modules and test activities/results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring and driving the team to deliver to the start our customer&#39;s require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or greater. An equivalent of at least 5 plus years&#39; of working experience in a DevOps capacity is also required for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have demonstrated the following competencies to the proficiency level appropriate to the seniority of the role:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Experience in deploying and operating infrastructure (network, servers, services) and applications on AWS and other cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and operating using open source and commercial software within a cloud-centric environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server build and administration, Linux and Windows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub/GitLab for source control and performing code reviews as part of the build and deployment cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD and Infrastructure-as-Code technologies, e.g. Terraform and Ansible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test Driven Development with appropriate tools and frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of cloud orchestration and containerisation technologies, such as Kubernetes and Docker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of large-scale databases and distributed technologies, such as RDS&lt;br&gt;Knowledge of distributed event streaming technologies, such as Kafka&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write/maintain automation script using Bash/Shell or python scripting languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of mentoring and leading people around you and taking point on key decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Aker Systems Attributes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Aker we work as a team; we are collaborative, hardworking, open, and delivery obsessed. There is no blame culture here: try things, and take responsibility for the outcomes. You are always part of the wider Aker. We help our colleagues and take pride in successfully achieving difficult tasks. We run towards problems and help to solve them. Communicate always, do so accurately and in a timely fashion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In return, we offer a competitive salary, 25 days holiday plus bank holidays, company paid medical insurance and life assurance, pension scheme, annual training allowance, wellbeing allowance, virtual GP, Employee Assistance plan and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aker Systems fosters a diverse environment that encourages openness in its communications and is committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people regardless of race, religion, gender or sexual orientation, age, marital status, national origin, citizenship status, disability, veteran status or other personal characteristics. We embrace differences of opinion and diversity because they help challenge us and find new groundbreaking technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Aker Systems was founded in 2017 by a team of experienced technology professionals who recognised an opportunity to provide highly secure enterprise data platforms to large organisations.&amp;nbsp; We build and operate ground-breaking, ultra-secure, high performance, cloud-based data infrastructure for the enterprise. Our proprietary technology solutions drive performance and reduce costs while helping our clients to improve the management and sharing of data across their organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2024, Aker Systems won the Breakthrough Culture Awards highlighting growth companies putting culture first. In 2020 Aker Systems was recognised as a ‘One to Watch’ on the Sunday Times Tech Track.&amp;nbsp; The Company was also recognised at the Thames Valley Tech Awards 2020; winning the Thames Valley Tech Company of the year, the Emerging Tech Company and High Growth Tech Business categories.&amp;nbsp; We encourage people of all different backgrounds and identities to apply.&amp;nbsp; We are committed to maintaining an inclusive, and supportive place for you to do your very best work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Location&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;UK / Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clearance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the client assignment, UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance may be required. Where SC clearance is required, candidates who do not currently hold clearance may be supported through the application process, subject to eligibility requirements, including having lived and worked in the UK for a minimum of 5 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Data Platform Engineer to provide hands-on technical leadership in designing, building and evolving secure, scalable and reliable data platforms for clients across the public sector and utilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across cloud-native and distributed data platforms, helping engineering teams build reliable platform capabilities that support batch, real-time streaming, analytical and operational workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines hands-on engineering with technical leadership. You will contribute to platform architecture and design decisions, establish engineering standards, solve complex technical challenges and work closely with architects, engineers and client stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience with cloud platforms, distributed systems and data platform engineering is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development and evolution of secure, scalable data platform services and components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement platform capabilities supporting batch, real-time streaming and hybrid workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise distributed data services using technologies such as Kafka, Kinesis, Spark, Flink or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform architecture and technical design decisions, balancing scalability, security, performance and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with architects and engineers to establish reusable platform patterns, standards and engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop cloud-native data platform capabilities using AWS and/or Azure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support high availability, fault tolerance, resilience and low-latency performance across platform services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain approaches to data modelling, schema management, data quality and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive engineering best practices including CI/CD, automated testing, TDD, observability and Infrastructure as Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support platform monitoring, troubleshooting, performance optimisation and root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to resilience, disaster recovery and operational readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with DevOps and Platform Engineering teams to improve deployment and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technical discovery and solution design with client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance, mentoring and support to Senior Data and Platform Engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks, dependencies and opportunities for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential Technical Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial experience in Data Platform Engineering, Data Engineering, Software Engineering or a similar technical discipline, with experience operating at Lead level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and building cloud-native, distributed data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Java and/or Python or equivalent modern programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with streaming and event-driven architectures, including Kafka, Kinesis or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale data processing technologies such as Spark, Flink, Kafka Streams or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with AWS and/or Azure cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS services such as S3, Lambda, Glue, RDS, Athena, EC2 and IAM is desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data pipeline architecture, orchestration and optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational and NoSQL databases, including data modelling and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing CI/CD, automated testing, observability and platform reliability practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of DevOps and Infrastructure as Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitHub/GitLab or equivalent source control platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile and/or DevOps environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desirable: Terraform, Docker, Kubernetes, Ansible, Packer, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Jenkins, GitLab CI, Python, Bash or Linux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within public sector, utilities or other regulated environments is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Data Platform Engineer, you will provide technical leadership within delivery teams and platform engineering activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical delivery of data platform capabilities and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform architecture, technical design and technology decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reusable engineering patterns and promote consistent technical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and mentor Senior Data and Platform Engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with architects, developers, DevOps and client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical debt, platform risks and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote secure, scalable, observable and maintainable engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support teams in balancing technical quality with delivery timelines and client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform resilience, operational readiness and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Engineering or a related technical discipline is desirable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should have 5+ years of relevant professional experience across Data Engineering, Software Engineering, Platform Engineering or a similar technical discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a Lead-level appointment, you should demonstrate experience taking ownership of complex platform engineering solutions, technical decisions and mentoring or guiding other engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security Clearance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Where required by the client assignment, UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance may be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates who do not currently hold SC clearance may be supported through the clearance process, subject to eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About You&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on platform engineer who understands how to build reliable data infrastructure that works in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You enjoy solving complex problems across cloud, distributed systems, streaming, data platforms and infrastructure, and can translate architectural requirements into practical engineering solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are comfortable moving between hands-on development, technical design and stakeholder discussions, while helping other engineers improve their technical capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You care about reliability, scalability, security, observability and maintainability, not simply getting a platform into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working within public sector, utilities or other complex and regulated environments would be highly advantageous.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Aker Systems Attributes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Aker we work as a team; we are collaborative, hardworking, open, and delivery obsessed. There is no blame culture here: try things, and take responsibility for the outcomes. You are always part of the wider Aker. We help our colleagues and take pride in successfully achieving difficult tasks. We run towards problems and help to solve them. Communicate always, do so accurately and in a timely fashion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In return, we offer a competitive salary, 25 days holiday plus bank holidays, company paid medical insurance and life assurance, pension scheme, annual training allowance, wellbeing allowance, virtual GP, Employee Assistance plan and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aker Systems fosters a diverse environment that encourages openness in its communications and is committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people regardless of race, religion, gender or sexual orientation, age, marital status, national origin, citizenship status, disability, veteran status or other personal characteristics. We embrace differences of opinion and diversity because they help challenge us and find new groundbreaking technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

